WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:15.677
Mrs. Rice: I was right all along!

2
00:00:15.678 --> 00:00:17.929
Mrs. Rice: I must open this garage door.

3
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.287
Why won't it open?

4
00:00:20.288 --> 00:00:22.757
Mrs. Rice: The giant must have locked the door.

5
00:00:22.758 --> 00:00:25.288
Tina might be inside.

6
00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:32.584
Mrs. Rice: Oh no, that means she is trapped inside with the giant!

7
00:00:32.585 --> 00:00:34.735
Mr. Joseph: Who is that on my driveway?

8
00:00:34.736 --> 00:00:36.959
I wonder what she wants.

9
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.083
Mrs. Rice: Finally, here comes someone who can help me.

10
00:00:41.084 --> 00:00:42.671
Mr. Joseph: Can I help you?

11
00:00:42.672 --> 00:00:45.990
Mrs. Rice: Thank goodness you're here.

12
00:00:45.991 --> 00:00:47.958
Mr. Joseph: What do you mean?

13
00:00:47.959 --> 00:00:49.467
What's going on?

14
00:00:49.468 --> 00:00:52.381
Mrs. Rice: I need you to help me open this garage door.

15
00:00:52.382 --> 00:00:54.339
We have to hurry.

16
00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:55.882
Mr. Joseph: Excuse me?

17
00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:58.448
Why do you need to open my garage?

18
00:00:58.449 --> 00:01:00.542
Mrs. Rice: Is this your garage?

19
00:01:00.543 --> 00:01:04.828
Oh good. That will make it easier.

20
00:01:04.829 --> 00:01:07.144
Mr. Joseph: Yes, yes, I live here.

21
00:01:07.145 --> 00:01:08.777
This is my house.

22
00:01:08.778 --> 00:01:13.035
Mr. Joseph: Now tell me, who you are and why you are trying to open my garage.

23
00:01:13.036 --> 00:01:15.024
Mrs. Rice: My name is Mrs. Rice.

24
00:01:15.025 --> 00:01:17.762
I live around the corner on the next street.

25
00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:20.227
Mrs. Rice: I'm Tina's neighbor.

26
00:01:20.228 --> 00:01:24.002
Mrs. Rice: I think she's trapped inside your garage and there's a─

27
00:01:24.003 --> 00:01:26.605
Mr. Joseph: Tina is a friend of my son Brad.

28
00:01:26.606 --> 00:01:30.741
Mr. Joseph: She and Brad are probably just playing [n3@inside the garage, that's all.

29
00:01:30.742 --> 00:01:33.726
Mr. Joseph: I'll bet Danny is with them.

30
00:01:33.727 --> 00:01:38.051
Mrs. Rice: Three children! Oh no, it's worse than I thought.

31
00:01:38.052 --> 00:01:40.148
Mr. Joseph: Don't get so excited.

32
00:01:40.149 --> 00:01:45.429
I'm sure there is nothing to worry about.

33
00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.805
Mr. Joseph: Hmm, it seems to be locked from the inside.

34
00:01:48.806 --> 00:01:50.160
Mr. Joseph: Follow me.

35
00:01:50.161 --> 00:01:59.665
We'll go around to the other door.

36
00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:01.193
Mr. Joseph: Please, come in.

37
00:02:01.194 --> 00:02:03.495
Mrs. Rice: Thank you.

38
00:02:03.496 --> 00:02:06.398
Mr. Joseph: We'll get this sorted out in no time.

39
00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:12.209
Mr. Joseph: The door to the garage is this way.

40
00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:16.000
Mr. Joseph: This is the door to the garage.

41
00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:19.061
Mr. Joseph: That's weird. This door is locked too.

42
00:02:19.062 --> 00:02:20.551
Mrs. Rice: I told you.

43
00:02:20.552 --> 00:02:24.074
An evil giant has trapped them inside the garage.

44
00:02:24.075 --> 00:02:29.150
Mr. Joseph: A giant? What on earth are you talking about, Mrs. Rice?

45
00:02:29.151 --> 00:02:34.102
Mrs. Rice: It's true. I saw Tina with a green, invisible giant.

46
00:02:34.103 --> 00:02:37.478
Mr. Joseph: If it was invisible, how could you see it?

47
00:02:37.479 --> 00:02:41.313
Mrs. Rice: I'm serious. There's an evil giant in there!

48
00:02:41.314 --> 00:02:43.020
Mr. Joseph: I don't think so.

49
00:02:43.021 --> 00:02:46.162
It's probably just my son and his friends.

50
00:02:46.163 --> 00:02:48.481
Mr. Joseph: You must have heard them playing a game.

51
00:02:48.482 --> 00:02:51.752
Mr. Joseph: They have very active imaginations.

52
00:02:51.753 --> 00:02:54.416
Mrs. Rice: I know a giant when I see one.

53
00:02:54.417 --> 00:02:58.208
And I'm telling you that I saw one!

54
00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:00.380
Mr. Joseph: Calm down, calm down.

55
00:03:00.381 --> 00:03:03.016
I'm sure there is an explanation.

56
00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:08.085
Mrs. Rice: You wouldn't be so calm if you saw a giant!

57
00:03:08.086 --> 00:03:09.906
Danny: Okay, I'm ready.

58
00:03:09.907 --> 00:03:13.264
Try it again, Brad.

59
00:03:13.265 --> 00:03:15.302
Brad: There, it's all set.

60
00:03:15.303 --> 00:03:23.471
This time it should restore Danny to normal size.

61
00:03:23.472 --> 00:03:25.225
Bello: What's the matter?

62
00:03:25.226 --> 00:03:27.234
Brad: This isn't going to work.

63
00:03:27.235 --> 00:03:28.943
I need to back up.

64
00:03:28.944 --> 00:03:34.098
Just a little bit further.

65
00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:41.277
Brad: Perfect. One, two, three . . .

66
00:03:41.278 --> 00:03:48.478
Mr. Joseph: Brad? Are you and your friends in there?

67
00:03:48.479 --> 00:03:50.767
Mrs. Rice: Did you see that?!

68
00:03:50.768 --> 00:03:56.361
Mr. Joseph: Bradley Joseph! What is going on in there?
